## 7. Conclusion

Dynatrace Grail and DQL were used to analyze eight application log events.

The DQL analysis identified `order-service` running on `k8s-worker-node-02` as the main failing component. This service-host combination generated three of the four ERROR events, representing 75% of all errors.

The three root-cause exceptions were:

- `DatabaseConnectionTimeout`
- `NullPointerException`
- `OutOfMemoryError`

The event-type analysis also identified three `app_crash` events, two `audit` events, one `network_timeout`, one `performance_warning`, and one `retry` event.

The recommended actions are to investigate the database connection pool, correct payload-validation defects, review JVM Metaspace usage, and configure Dynatrace alerts for repeated service errors and application crashes.
